  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Opening a two-axis or radial puppet in certain worlds causes my avatar to stop moving for others. They can still hear me, and I can still see everything updating as expected, and as soon as I close the puppet, any changes that I made will update for them, but while the puppet is open, it's like all information about my avatar's state and motion stops propagating to everyone else.\nExample world where it happens: https://vrchat.com/home/launch?worldId=wrld_e5db4faf-fff9-4a92-a150-cb3439e5d742\nI have no idea what sort of world setting could cause this, or if it's intentional that puppets are moved to a lower priority sync, but there should be no reason that the entire avatar freezes - even head, hand, and locomotion movements aren't propagated to other clients.",
